<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <fullName>Outcome__c</fullName>
    <externalId>false</externalId>
    <label>Outcome</label>
    <length>255</length>
    <required>false</required>
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description>, AND IT MUST STAY THAT WAY.
        `CustomField.Description` is capped at 1000 characters. The text below had grown to
        1126 and made this file UNDEPLOYABLE from source — a live dry-run validation deploy
        against usman-dpeg (classes plus this object, 313 components) returned exactly one
        error: "Inbound_Email_Staging__c.Outcome__c: Value too long for field: Description
        maximum length is:1000" (found 2026-08-05; pre-existing and unrelated to the
        attachment-capture feature landing the same day — this file was byte-identical at
        HEAD and in the worktree, so it was committed but never previously deployed from
        source). The content is genuinely load-bearing, so it was moved rather than trimmed;
        a comment is repo-only and never sent to the Metadata API, so it can be as long as it
        needs to be. Same convention as Broker_Protection_Access.permissionset-meta.xml.
        Do not paste this back into <description>.

        RETIRED LABELS: rows created before 2026-07-31 may carry the retired labels
        'Competing Duplicate' / 'Competing Duplicate (race)', superseded by 'Competing
        Submission' / 'Competing Submission (race)'.

        FULL GATE DETAIL for 'Not Routed (call for offers)' (Intake Rules V2 U2, added
        2026-08-03): the LLM classified the email as a marketed call-for-offers campaign,
        which DPEG does not work. Gated post-callout and unconditionally — no toggle and no
        confidence threshold. Creates no Lead and no Property_Registry__c claim, but still
        logs a Task, and the staging row retains the raw body and the full Extracted_JSON__c
        so nothing is lost. Findable via the Gated_Call_For_Offers list view.

        SUFFIX DETAIL for multi-property outcome strings ('Multi-Property (N): ...'): they may
        carry ' [truncated: X of M]' when more properties were found in the email than
        MAX_PROPERTIES, or ' [unclaimed: lock timeout]' when a property failed safe under lock
        contention.
    -->
    <description>Routing outcome label (e.g., 'New Lead (winner)', 'Competing Submission', 'Reply Thread'). Gate labels: 'Not Acquisition (gated)' (LLM classifier hard gate), 'Not Acquisition (pre-filtered)' (deterministic pre-filter, no LLM callout), 'Not Routed (call for offers)' (Intake Rules V2 U2, marketed call-for-offers campaign). Multi-property emails (2026-07-31+) use prefix 'Multi-Property (N): ...' summarizing each property's outcome, with optional suffixes ' [truncated: X of M]' or ' [unclaimed: lock timeout]'. See in-root XML comment for retired labels and full gate/suffix detail.</description>
    <type>Text</type>
</CustomField>
